> This recipe is intended to use up leftovers. Ingredients can be substituted as required.

Purée half of the @cannellini beans{1%tin × 400 g} with all of the liquid from the can.

Heat the @sunflower oil{2%tbsp} in a #large frying pan{} on a medium heat, then saute the @red onions{2} until they soften. Add the @carrots{2}(finely chopped), @celery{2%sticks}(finely chopped), and @salt{pinch}, and cook until soft.

Add the @leek{1}(thickly sliced), @squash{200%g}(peeled and cut into rough 1 cm chunks), @savoy cabbage outer leaves (or other greens){250%g}(shredded), @garlic{2%cloves}(peeled, squashed, and finely chopped), @fennel seeds{1%tsp}, and @chilli flakes{1%tsp}. Cover and cook until limp, stirring occasionally.

Add the @chopped tomatoes{1%tin × 400 g}, puréed beans, and the @wine, stock, or water{250%ml}. Cover again and leave to bubble for about ~{40%minutes}, or until the vegetables are cooked to taste.

Stir in the remaining beans and the @stale bread{200%g}. Cook until the latter is soft, then season to taste with @salt and @pepper.

Optionally drizzle with @?olive oil{} and pop under a hot grill until crisp on top.

Top with @grated cheese{} and @?spring onions{2}.